Z||000000||making it better||03-16-2000||11:37 PM||||'87 Fiero GT.  Looking to spend $2000 can. or $1500 US.  Questioning best way to 200hp without nitro.  wonder which is better Pisa stroker kit and/or boring it to 3.1 or using Dennis Lagura turbo idea. or do you have a better idea ||||reg||1
Z||000001||87SC/GT||03-16-2000||11:56 PM||||I spend many an hour pondering the same question. A turbo effectively fools the engine into thinking it is of much larger displacement. It does not really rob mechanical energy like a supercharger. I am leaning towards a 3.1 rebuild using the rebuild kit made for the 89-90 Pontiac Turbo Grand Prix. It is about 350.00 US through Northern Auto Parts . <A HREF="http://www.naparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.naparts.com</A> <BR>Dennis's site tells you most of the other things you need to know. You will need a MAP sensor from a turbo GM and probably a custom chip burned but it can all be done. I am putting together the pieces from information gained right here. The IHI turbo from the Mustang/Tbird is not the best choice of turbo but it is probably the cheapest and most plentiful. You are better to get a turbo from a slightly smaller engine than a larger engine. Also try to use one with an integral wastegate. The external wastegates cost a fortune. Cheers   Sorry for the book! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||03-17-2000||11:27 AM||||So you will be switching to the aluminum heads and induction?||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||03-17-2000||04:47 PM||||SC/GT,<P>The Garrett/Air Research turbos that are prevalent on Chrysler products often seem to be a good match.  They are always in the T2 to T2.5 range which is a good size for our engine.  <P>Otherwise rob a Mitsu.  They both offer an integral wastegate. <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000004||fastonpumpgas||03-17-2000||05:46 PM||||you wont get 200 ho for 1500 us dollars, you can try though, the 3.1 would be 1500 alone and you might get 160 out of that||||reg||1
